      "widgets_values": [
        "IMAGE TO VIDEO — the finale: the whole pack in one graph.\n\nThe Generator paints a keyframe; the Video Generator (wan-2-2) animates it. With an image wired in, the video PROMPT describes MOTION, not content — camera moves, what drifts, what shimmers. The image already says what everything looks like.\n\nPATIENCE REQUIRED: video renders on ASU's servers for ~5 minutes for a 4-second clip. The progress bar is real — let it run.\n\nYou can also disconnect the image input entirely: the node then does text-to-video and the prompt describes both content AND motion.\n\nMOTION PROMPT CRAFT: one camera instruction + two or three subject motions is plenty. 'Everything moves' reads as chaos.\n\nEXERCISE: storyboard a 3-shot sequence. Generate three keyframes with workflow 01, animate each with a different camera move, and cut them together."
      ],
